     "user": "Design a low-carbon grout paste: mini-slump flow diameter >= 200 mm and 7-day compressive strength >= 30 MPa, minimise CO2. Space: w/b 0.30-0.50, OPC required, class F fly ash 0-0.5. Run without asking.",
     "text": "I’ll run the inverse design for your specified targets and search space, minimizing CO₂, and check published analogues for the flow prediction.\n**Best screened candidate: OPC/Class F fly ash ≈ 0.92/0.08 by binder mass, w/b = 0.318.** This is a trial mix, not a verified optimum.\n\n| Property | Prediction: q50 [q10, q90] | Target |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Mini-slump diameter | 201.4 [94.5, 289.6] mm | ≥200 mm |\n| Compressive strength, 7 days | 35.0 [22.5, 68.9] MPa | ≥30 MPa |\n\nEstimated CO₂: **0.782 kg CO₂/kg binder**, or **1,188 kg CO₂/m³ paste**, using the engine’s factors. Estimated joint target satisfaction is only **35.2%**, assuming independence. Lower-carbon returned candidates failed the screening thresholds.\n\nAssumptions: moist curing, `comp_cube50` specimens, non-3DCP paste, no aggregate or admixtures. Screening required satisfaction probabilities of 0.50 for flow and 0.60 for strength.\n\n**Published evidence takes priority for flow:** the mini-slump model is weak, so its prediction is order-of-magnitude guidance. Retrieved analogue [M1](https://doi.org/10.3389/fmats.2021.712551) reports OPC/Class F fly ash = 0.85/0.15, w/b = 0.30, and PCE = 0.50% of binder, with measured mini-slump **268 mm** and 7-day strength **82 MPa**. Its added PCE differs from this search’s assumptions; verify the full formulation and test protocol before replication.\n\nThe models describe literature correlations; experimentally verify both targets before adopting the mix.\n\nFiles: [report](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-170944-97ae/design_Low-carbon grout paste/report.md>), [candidates](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-170944-97ae/design_Low-carbon grout paste/candidates.csv>), [literature](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-170944-97ae/literature.csv>), [Pareto figure](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifact